# SecPivot line-ending policy
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enforce LF for every text file on BOTH commit (normalize to LF) and checkout.
# This keeps the repository consistent across platforms. Windows CI checks out
# with core.autocrlf by default, which produced CRLF working trees and broke
# the source-structure regex tests (e.g. the global auto-type contract). The
# explicit eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf for every text file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalized or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.bmp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.pdf binary
*.sqlite binary
*.db binary
